WEBVTT

00:03.720 --> 00:07.980
<i>Having bidden a temporary farewell to 
academy life due to the end-of-term break,</i>

00:08.480 --> 00:11.880
<i>Princess Mia was on the 
road home to the empire.</i>

00:11.880 --> 00:17.140
Oh, out of the head chef's kindness, 
my last meal has become lavish!

00:17.140 --> 00:19.370
Now it says it's Yellow Moon tomato stew!

00:23.220 --> 00:27.080
Whoa, whoa, whoa, that means 
I'm still headed to the guillotine!

00:27.560 --> 00:31.800
It looks like the largest factor is 
the food shortage due to crop failure.

00:31.800 --> 00:34.640
This part also stands out.

00:34.640 --> 00:38.890
A conflict with a isolated tribe 
in a remote border forest.

00:40.590 --> 00:42.540
I feel sick...

00:43.270 --> 00:46.000
Anne! Anne!

00:46.000 --> 00:47.440
What is it?

00:48.370 --> 00:49.430
I feel nauseous...

00:49.430 --> 00:51.120
You're carriage-sick?!

00:52.730 --> 00:56.390
Ah! Princess Mia!

02:27.000 --> 02:31.670
<b>Episode 7: Princess Mia Sees Clearly</b>

02:32.640 --> 02:35.380
It is good to see you well 
after so long, Your Highness.

02:35.380 --> 02:39.090
I'm glad to see you in good 
health as well, Ludwig.

02:41.550 --> 02:44.740
Our food reserves are not nearly sufficient.

02:44.740 --> 02:48.230
Any more and the storage costs alone 
would put pressure on imperial finances.

02:48.470 --> 02:54.060
<i>Ah, it's so frustrating that I can't say 
there will be a famine in a few years!</i>

02:54.270 --> 02:58.280
Then if a famine should occur,
 what could we do?

02:58.280 --> 03:02.670
Typically, the only option would be to 
have merchants import food.

03:02.670 --> 03:06.040
Though it's certain that they 
would force exorbitant prices.

03:06.490 --> 03:10.550
<i>It's not as though one day all the 
food in the world will disappear.</i>

03:10.550 --> 03:12.810
<i>Some places will have food.</i>

03:12.810 --> 03:14.380
<i>Which means...</i>

03:14.880 --> 03:16.130
I've got it!

03:16.510 --> 03:18.340
Friend prices.

03:18.790 --> 03:20.870
Friend... prices?

03:22.380 --> 03:25.260
It's a pleasure to meet you, Your Highness.

03:25.260 --> 03:29.350
I am Chloe's father, Marco Forkroad.

03:29.600 --> 03:32.810
Welcome, Lord Forkroad.

03:33.430 --> 03:37.440
<i>I sent my daughter to Saint Noel 
Academy to benefit her future.</i>

03:37.440 --> 03:42.210
<i>But I never dreamed she'd become friends 
with the princess of a major empire!</i>

03:42.210 --> 03:44.450
<i>And what even is a "reading buddy" anyway?</i>

03:44.660 --> 03:46.610
I trust Chloe is doing well?

03:46.610 --> 03:49.330
Yes, she has her nose 
buried in books, as always.

03:49.680 --> 03:52.860
<i>In any event, this is a once-in-a-lifetime 
chance my daughter has given me.</i>

03:52.860 --> 03:55.430
Now then, I should like to inquire something.

03:55.430 --> 03:56.420
Y-Yes, Your Highness?

03:56.420 --> 04:00.760
Is it possible to have you 
import goods from overseas?

04:00.760 --> 04:03.140
Certainly, Your Highness.

04:03.140 --> 04:05.890
What goods would you desire?

04:05.890 --> 04:09.350
Spices? Or rugs, perhaps?

04:09.350 --> 04:11.430
Wheat is what I seek.

04:12.660 --> 04:14.900
<i>Why import that all the way from overseas?</i>

04:14.900 --> 04:16.900
This comes with certain conditions.

04:17.120 --> 04:21.610
Even if there should be a famine, 
no increase in price will be permitted.

04:21.940 --> 04:22.560
Wha—?!

04:22.990 --> 04:26.570
<i>Ridiculous! How would that benefit me?</i>

04:28.410 --> 04:34.120
<i>But from what Chloe says, Princess Mia 
isn't the sort to abuse her authority.</i>

04:34.380 --> 04:39.590
<i>For a friend of your daughter,
 you'll be a bit more accommodating, won't you?</i>

04:40.030 --> 04:42.970
<i>Could it be... I'm being tested?</i>

04:43.240 --> 04:44.990
Ah, lest I forget.

04:44.990 --> 04:49.050
I would always purchase a 
minimum amount of wheat.

04:50.520 --> 04:52.430
<i>I accidentally forgot to include that detail.</i>

04:52.820 --> 04:55.890
<i>Ludwig told me to mention it.</i>

04:55.890 --> 05:01.190
<i>No matter the circumstances, 
she'd pay a fixed amount at a fixed price...</i>

05:00.440 --> 05:04.860
<b>Price</b>

05:00.440 --> 05:04.860
<b>Delivery Date</b>

05:01.190 --> 05:04.860
<i>Meaning it would never be affected 
by changes in goods prices.</i>

05:04.860 --> 05:07.120
If the wheat is to be imported from overseas,

05:07.120 --> 05:09.830
the price would have to be set fairly high.

05:09.830 --> 05:12.910
What are Your Highness's 
thoughts regarding that?

05:14.260 --> 05:17.220
This details the specifics of the contract.

05:19.820 --> 05:22.990
<i>The price is exceedingly low 
compared to famine prices...</i>

05:22.990 --> 05:26.200
<i>I completely left the 
price decision to Ludwig.</i>

05:26.200 --> 05:28.470
<i>I hope that was the right move...</i>

05:28.470 --> 05:32.320
<i>This price... is fantastic!</i>

05:32.320 --> 05:34.060
<i>It guarantees plenty of profit.</i>

05:34.480 --> 05:37.840
<i>I see. In exchange for an 
elevated price in normal times,</i>

05:37.840 --> 05:39.860
<i>I'm to be accommodating during a shortage.</i>

05:40.370 --> 05:46.870
<i>It guarantees my interests even as it builds 
a system to prevent her people's starvation...</i>

05:46.870 --> 05:49.030
<i>What an astounding individual.</i>

05:49.420 --> 05:53.130
<i>By "friend prices," she meant
 providing benefits for friends.</i>

05:53.130 --> 05:54.820
<i>She's taking on the role of the villain,</i>

05:54.820 --> 05:57.630
<i>indicating what will be 
considered the permissible range,</i>

05:57.630 --> 06:01.960
<i>and loosening the reins on the 
nobility that I had held too tight.</i>

06:02.490 --> 06:05.140
<i>This is the Wisdom of the Empire!</i>

06:06.690 --> 06:12.050
<i>Thanks to several unique misunderstandings, 
everything wrapped up nicely.</i>

06:14.150 --> 06:17.660
<i>At a later date, Mia decided to make 
a visit to the New Moon District,</i>

06:17.660 --> 06:20.600
<i>the slum she had visited before.</i>

06:20.600 --> 06:24.460
Is it just me, or has the 
atmosphere here changed?

06:24.460 --> 06:28.810
Now that the hospital has begun 
operating and food provisions doubled,

06:28.810 --> 06:31.220
it appears vitality is gradually returning.

06:31.220 --> 06:33.080
I'm so glad to see that!

06:34.740 --> 06:35.700
Your Highness!

06:35.970 --> 06:38.660
Oh? I remember you...

06:40.900 --> 06:43.440
It appears you're all better now.

06:43.440 --> 06:46.910
Yes. Thanks to you, Your Highness. Thank you!

06:47.760 --> 06:50.050
Take this. As thanks for saving me.

06:50.740 --> 06:51.660
What is it?

06:52.450 --> 06:54.130
A unicorn hairpin.

06:54.130 --> 06:56.670
Oh, my! Unicorn?

06:56.670 --> 06:58.890
It's made from a tree in my homeland.

06:58.890 --> 07:01.100
This is lovely.

07:03.740 --> 07:06.360
Thank you. This makes me very happy.

07:08.430 --> 07:09.610
B-Bye now!

07:10.410 --> 07:13.320
That hairpin is a memento 
from the child's mother.

07:15.810 --> 07:19.680
So, what did you mean when you 
said this hairpin was a memento?

07:19.680 --> 07:22.580
His mother is from a small tribe

07:22.580 --> 07:26.590
that lives in a remote forest of the empire
 known as the Forest of Stillness.

07:26.960 --> 07:31.940
She fell in love with a man from another tribe, 
and they essentially eloped to the capital.

07:31.940 --> 07:35.680
Then she perished from illness 
when that boy was still very young.

07:35.680 --> 07:40.320
W-Would this tribe happen to be the Lulus?

07:40.320 --> 07:42.770
I should have known Your Highness 
would be aware of them.

07:43.420 --> 07:48.130
<i>The Lulus are the tribe that 
Tiona's servant, Liora, comes from.</i>

07:48.130 --> 07:53.300
<i>According to my diary, a regional conflict 
occurs between the empire and that tribe.</i>

07:53.300 --> 07:57.280
<i>It's no wonder Tiona developed 
a negative impression of me!</i>

07:57.280 --> 08:00.250
<i>The best option would be to 
have nothing to do with this!</i>

08:00.540 --> 08:05.010
I couldn't possibly accept 
something so precious.

08:05.010 --> 08:07.210
No, please do take it.

08:07.210 --> 08:07.920
What?

08:07.920 --> 08:13.160
Ever since you saved him, that child 
has been saying he'd like to thank you.

08:13.160 --> 08:16.700
That hairpin is his heartfelt gift to you.

08:17.730 --> 08:23.520
<i>I'll have to take the opposite track, then, 
and build friendly relations with the boy!</i>

08:23.760 --> 08:26.650
I'll wear it every day!

08:27.810 --> 08:33.370
<i>Little did Mia know that this act would 
have unexpected effects on the future.</i>

08:34.300 --> 08:39.790
<i>Meanwhile, in the southeast of the empire, 
at the Berman Estate in Viscount Berman's lands...</i>

08:41.230 --> 08:43.370
Outland Count Rudolvon...

08:43.570 --> 08:46.710
That infuriating country noble!

08:47.180 --> 08:52.130
<i>The impetus was a truly foolish 
exchange at a certain party.</i>

08:52.460 --> 08:54.720
You know Viscount Berman,

08:54.720 --> 09:00.850
I simply cannot comprehend how an outland 
count like Rudolvon can have more land than you,

09:01.140 --> 09:06.850
a member of the illustrious 
central aristocracy.

09:07.610 --> 09:11.520
The Outland Count's lands are all 
either farmland or forested areas.

09:11.520 --> 09:14.320
The amount of such land is 
surely nothing to boast of.

09:14.320 --> 09:16.610
Even so, my good viscount...

09:17.100 --> 09:19.030
If I were in your situation,

09:19.030 --> 09:23.250
I should desire not to be inferior to 
such a <i>rustic</i> noble in <i>any</i> respect.

09:25.280 --> 09:27.370
I do have an insight to share.

09:28.110 --> 09:31.200
You need simply develop the Forest of Stillness.

09:31.200 --> 09:33.180
The Forest of Stillness, you say?

09:33.960 --> 09:37.670
<i>On the border of Viscount Berman 
and Outland Count Rudolvon's lands</i>

09:37.670 --> 09:41.970
<i>was a vast forested area 
known as the Forest of Stillness.</i>

09:41.970 --> 09:45.020
<i>which made the border 
between the two ambiguous.</i>

09:45.020 --> 09:50.060
<i>And so Berman aimed to expand 
his lands by developing the forest.</i>

09:50.060 --> 09:52.650
<i>But a problem arose.</i>

09:52.650 --> 09:57.500
<i>The Lulus, who lived in that forest, 
took on a posture of total resistance.</i>

09:57.500 --> 10:03.530
<i>In a panic, Berman bribed military authorities 
to dispatch a century of soldiers.</i>

10:03.530 --> 10:05.710
<i>But the centurion in command</i>

10:05.710 --> 10:07.580
<i>used maintenance of peace and 
public order as a reason</i>

10:07.580 --> 10:09.650
<i>to completely refrain 
from invading the forest.</i>

10:09.650 --> 10:13.170
<i>Berman's irritation was 
rising towards its apex.</i>

10:13.400 --> 10:19.010
Curses. In that case, 
I'll go even higher over your head.

10:21.470 --> 10:26.560
Princess Mia, your hair has become
 noticeably glossier recently!

10:27.720 --> 10:29.980
Yes, I imagine it has.

10:29.980 --> 10:33.680
This shampoo Prince Abel 
graciously gifted to me...

10:33.680 --> 10:35.990
It doesn't just remove dirt and grime,

10:35.990 --> 10:39.280
but also bestows nutrients and 
a lustrous sheen to the hair.

10:39.280 --> 10:41.000
I think you'll like it.

10:44.400 --> 10:47.450
I hope Princess Mia's favorite 
horse becomes glossy like mine.

10:49.370 --> 10:54.330
<i>It's just like Prince Abel to 
give such a wonderful present.</i>

10:54.330 --> 10:56.960
<i>It was horse shampoo.</i>

10:57.280 --> 11:00.570
A pleasure to make your 
acquaintance, Viscount Berman.

11:01.920 --> 11:04.940
Goodness. How beautiful!

11:04.940 --> 11:07.930
Though your entire appearance 
is lovely, those lustrous locks!

11:07.930 --> 11:11.900
They shine like the coat of a famed 
horse galloping across the battlefield!

11:11.900 --> 11:15.320
Oh, my! Aren't you silver-tongued!

11:15.320 --> 11:17.860
<i>He's not exactly wrong.</i>

11:19.190 --> 11:21.570
<i>I see she's simply a selfish young girl...</i>

11:21.570 --> 11:24.740
Oh, is that a unicorn hairpin?

11:24.740 --> 11:26.030
It truly suits Your Highness.

11:26.380 --> 11:29.120
I wear it practically every day.

11:29.390 --> 11:33.960
You know, that hairpin is made from 
a tree of a certain forest.

11:34.340 --> 11:37.170
The Forest of Stillness, I believe it was.

11:37.170 --> 11:39.050
So Your Highness has heard of it!

11:40.370 --> 11:41.600
How does this sound?

11:41.600 --> 11:44.730
On Your Highness's orders, 
I could develop that forest,

11:44.730 --> 11:46.960
and then you could have all the 
unicorn hairpins you'd like!

11:46.960 --> 11:49.980
I should very much like to visit that forest!

11:50.730 --> 11:51.440
What?

11:51.970 --> 11:54.680
Ludwig, I would set off right away.

11:54.680 --> 11:56.000
Make the arrangements.

11:57.150 --> 11:59.060
R-Right away?

11:59.060 --> 12:00.570
But...

12:08.580 --> 12:12.810
<i>Thanks to Viscount Berman, 
I have a pretext to go to the forest.</i>

12:12.810 --> 12:16.330
<i>I'll use this opportunity 
to befriend the Lulus!</i>

12:16.330 --> 12:19.530
<i>Mia remained stable in 
her Mia-first philosophy.</i>

12:19.530 --> 12:24.430
I'm impressed you arranged this 
so quickly after my order. Well done.

12:24.820 --> 12:29.610
This unit is the Princess Guard, a unit 
exclusively for your protection, Princess Mia.

12:29.610 --> 12:30.770
I formed it for you.

12:31.180 --> 12:33.970
The name has a lovely ring to it.

12:33.970 --> 12:35.640
Now then, Ludwig...

12:35.640 --> 12:36.230
Yes?

12:36.230 --> 12:40.190
Could you tell me more about 
Viscount Berman and his lands?

12:44.360 --> 12:47.190
<i>As a capable government official,</i>

12:47.190 --> 12:51.830
<i>Ludwig had firmly appraised the 
problems developing in Berman's lands.</i>

12:52.740 --> 12:55.290
<i>Oh, shit!</i>

12:55.290 --> 12:58.340
<i>Unrefined language crept 
into her internal monologue.</i>

12:58.340 --> 13:02.360
<i>Such was the crossroads of fate 
where Mia found herself standing.</i>

13:02.930 --> 13:06.890
<i>The Forest of Stillness gets 
developed to procure materials.</i>

13:06.890 --> 13:09.600
<i>For that purpose, the Lulus are removed.</i>

13:09.600 --> 13:13.020
<i>And just beyond the forest are 
Outland Count Rudolvon's lands...</i>

13:13.410 --> 13:16.480
<i>Danger words are springing up left and right!</i>

13:16.730 --> 13:21.970
<i>It's written in my diary that my 
relationship with Tiona sours.</i>

13:23.560 --> 13:24.780
Princess Mia.

13:25.090 --> 13:27.950
I've solved all the puzzles.

13:27.950 --> 13:31.120
Viscount Berman's acts are inexcusable! 
Royally inexcusable!

13:31.470 --> 13:35.540
<i>As I thought, she isn't one to tolerate 
the tyrannies of the aristocracy.</i>

13:36.100 --> 13:38.540
So then, what does 
Your Highness intend to do?

13:39.440 --> 13:41.220
The answer is clear!

13:41.220 --> 13:43.000
I'll crush his plans!

13:52.370 --> 13:56.890
Another written demand 
from Viscount Berman, sir?

13:58.230 --> 14:03.490
Good grief. I swear, nobles tell people 
to kill and risk their lives so easily.

14:03.490 --> 14:05.010
Must be nice to be so carefree.

14:05.010 --> 14:06.950
I get how you feel, sir.

14:06.950 --> 14:10.640
Our mission is only to maintain public order.

14:10.640 --> 14:14.590
Indeed. I'm not about to 
send my men to die in vain.

14:14.590 --> 14:16.580
Fighting in this forest is too dangerous.

14:17.090 --> 14:20.260
It would only be you and me that 
might make it back alive.

14:21.240 --> 14:25.100
For only the commander and his deputy 
to survive... That ain't a good look.

14:28.470 --> 14:30.700
Imperial guards?

14:30.700 --> 14:34.600
Word is the imperial princess 
herself is making a visit.

14:34.600 --> 14:36.100
Really now?

14:36.100 --> 14:39.440
So you think it smells fishy, too, sir?

14:39.710 --> 14:43.770
I would image the viscount brought 
her here from the capital.

14:43.770 --> 14:47.150
Who knows what nonsense he fed her?

14:47.150 --> 14:52.310
Still, Her Highness is said 
to be extremely sharp.

14:52.310 --> 14:56.300
Things are never the way you want them to be.

14:56.300 --> 15:00.830
That's a pessimistic saying. 
What philosopher said that?

15:01.600 --> 15:02.550
Me.

15:20.100 --> 15:21.390
Princess Mia!

15:21.390 --> 15:22.970
Are you all right, Princess Mia?

15:22.970 --> 15:25.270
Princess Mia!

15:28.060 --> 15:33.780
Your selfish whims started the conflict with
 the Lulus in the Forest of Stillness.

15:34.450 --> 15:37.470
All my men died in the fighting there.

15:38.160 --> 15:40.540
I'll see you pay for that.

15:42.660 --> 15:43.700
No!

15:45.370 --> 15:48.200
Princess Mia! How do you feel?

15:48.200 --> 15:52.190
The heat just got to me. That's all.

15:52.190 --> 15:53.660
I'm fine now.

15:53.660 --> 15:57.120
It is a pleasure to meet you, 
Your Highness. I am Dion Alaia.

15:57.680 --> 16:01.020
I have command over the soldiers 
the Imperial Army dispatched here.

16:01.020 --> 16:03.100
<i>We've already met.</i>

16:03.100 --> 16:06.610
<i>You cut my head clean off my shoulders!</i>

16:06.880 --> 16:08.680
Is there something on my face?

16:08.680 --> 16:10.860
N-No, it's nothing.

16:10.860 --> 16:14.470
I was just frightened by this 
veritable bear of a man.

16:15.400 --> 16:16.740
Like a bear, you say?

16:17.080 --> 16:21.420
Princess Mia, please visit the 
forest with Centurion Dion.

16:21.890 --> 16:22.870
What?

16:22.870 --> 16:25.100
I'll have one of your guards 
accompany you as well.

16:27.960 --> 16:30.840
<i>I swear. What on earth is this 
four-eyes going on about?</i>

16:30.840 --> 16:34.430
Mr. Ludwig, I'd appreciate you not 
just deciding what happens next.

16:34.430 --> 16:37.510
<i>Yes, that's right. You tell him!</i>

16:38.210 --> 16:40.400
The imperial guards' armor 
stands out too much.

16:40.400 --> 16:45.070
Can you take responsibility if it 
antagonizes the Lulus and starts a war?

16:45.070 --> 16:47.690
Yes. I'm aware of the risks.

16:47.690 --> 16:52.790
But we must take the risk to send 
Princess Mia into the forest in secret.

16:52.790 --> 16:54.990
That should give us the 
best read on the situation.

16:55.380 --> 16:59.080
<i>So that's just how highly 
he regards Her Highness...</i>

16:59.080 --> 17:02.790
Excuse me, what are you two discussing?

17:03.000 --> 17:07.130
Hm... Well if that's the situation, 
I suppose there's no other way.

17:08.040 --> 17:11.030
Then I trust you find this 
arrangement acceptable, Princess Mia.

17:11.760 --> 17:14.720
<i>It's not acceptable at all!</i>

17:17.340 --> 17:19.580
Are you all right, Your Highness?

17:19.580 --> 17:20.910
Oh. Yes!

17:23.180 --> 17:28.100
Is there really any reason to station 
soldiers here in the first place?

17:28.400 --> 17:29.560
None whatsoever.

17:29.560 --> 17:33.250
In fact, having them here only 
increases the risk of conflict.

17:33.250 --> 17:34.570
Then why even...

17:34.570 --> 17:38.560
Unfortunately, we were ordered to come here.

17:38.560 --> 17:40.480
Even though we know it would 
be better to withdraw,

17:40.480 --> 17:42.290
we can't do so without a proper reason.

17:43.360 --> 17:45.620
A proper reason to withdraw...

17:51.020 --> 17:52.440
Um, where are we now?

17:52.440 --> 17:55.300
We're now in the forest proper. 
We're on the front lines.

17:55.300 --> 17:56.930
Th-The front lines?!

17:57.290 --> 18:00.480
Do please refrain from carelessly 
touching anything in the forest.

18:00.480 --> 18:01.090
Oh?

18:01.090 --> 18:04.550
To them, these trees are precious assets.

18:04.550 --> 18:06.750
If you don't treat them properly...

18:06.750 --> 18:08.520
I-I've heard and seen enough!

18:08.520 --> 18:10.190
I want to go b-back—

18:13.640 --> 18:14.530
Your Highness!

18:14.530 --> 18:15.520
Are you all right?

18:15.520 --> 18:16.410
Are you hurt?

18:16.410 --> 18:18.340
Please be careful, Your Highness.

18:18.340 --> 18:21.970
It's the root's fault for 
sticking way out here.

18:23.870 --> 18:27.430
That's right! The tree 
is at fault. This tree!

18:27.430 --> 18:28.120
Your Highness?

18:29.250 --> 18:30.880
What an impudent tree!

18:43.810 --> 18:46.140
Fall back! Retreat to outside the forest!

18:49.590 --> 18:52.450
I shouldn't say this, Your Highness, 
but I could kill you!

18:53.970 --> 18:57.610
You heard me tell you not to carelessly 
touch anything in the forest, didn't you?

18:57.610 --> 19:00.160
W-W-W-We need to escape!

19:00.160 --> 19:03.490
No need to tell me.
 I'm already taking you back to camp.

19:03.490 --> 19:05.620
T-Take me back to the town!

19:05.620 --> 19:09.210
I won't feel safe unless we go all 
the way to the Viscount's estate!

19:09.210 --> 19:12.850
Then be my guest. Have your 
imperial guards take you there.

19:12.850 --> 19:14.420
I'll add one of my units to escort you.

19:14.420 --> 19:17.280
No, the entire force!

19:17.280 --> 19:17.900
What?

19:25.720 --> 19:27.150
That was close.

19:28.270 --> 19:29.500
This is an order.

19:29.500 --> 19:33.350
Gather all the troops to 
guard me and return to town.

19:34.570 --> 19:38.070
It takes some time to move 
an army, Your Highness.

19:38.070 --> 19:41.650
What task is more important 
than ensuring my safety?

19:44.430 --> 19:46.550
I shall do as you command, Your Highness.

19:46.550 --> 19:48.080
S-Sir?

19:48.880 --> 19:50.550
Inform all troops.

19:50.550 --> 19:53.220
We're shifting position to the town,

19:53.220 --> 19:56.700
in perfect file, as befits 
Her Illustrious Highness.

19:59.110 --> 20:02.380
Your Highness, what is the meaning of this?

20:02.920 --> 20:04.970
If this causes disruptions at the work site...

20:04.970 --> 20:09.480
Oh, are you suggesting, Lord Berman, 
that I make do with but a handful of guards?

20:09.480 --> 20:11.180
Is that it?

20:11.180 --> 20:14.440
N-Not at all, Your Highness. 
I-I would never...

20:14.440 --> 20:19.530
Oh, and one more thing. I wish to 
speak with my father about that land,

20:19.530 --> 20:23.570
so I shall have you refrain from any logging 
 or troop movements for the time being.

20:23.960 --> 20:25.320
I can't believe this.

20:25.320 --> 20:29.160
I'm afraid I must take my leave. 
I trust you to adhere to this.

20:30.960 --> 20:34.040
So you've finally secured 
a place for every soldier.

20:34.040 --> 20:36.650
It was pretty tough to make happen.

20:37.500 --> 20:38.800
Pardon me.

20:38.800 --> 20:40.360
Centurion Dion,

20:41.550 --> 20:45.300
I apologize for the great trouble 
Her Highness caused for you.

20:45.710 --> 20:48.390
Actually, I think Her Highness 
did me a huge favor.

20:48.390 --> 20:51.470
What? How do you mean?

20:51.750 --> 20:54.260
Don't you see? It was a bluff.

20:54.260 --> 20:55.210
A bluff?

20:55.210 --> 21:00.800
You mean, she kicked the tree on
 purpose to create an excuse to withdraw?

21:02.460 --> 21:04.430
So, you understand, right?

21:04.430 --> 21:05.200
Huh?

21:05.600 --> 21:10.020
Whether Her Highness's efforts 
go to waste depends on you.

21:11.120 --> 21:13.950
If His Majesty hears that the 
Lulus fired arrows at his daughter,

21:13.950 --> 21:16.290
he'll be forced to make a response.

21:16.800 --> 21:20.750
Which is why we mustn't breathe a word 
about what happened in the forest.

21:20.750 --> 21:23.170
Y-Yes, sir! Of course!

21:26.200 --> 21:29.040
Why am I coming to Princess Mia's defense?

21:31.250 --> 21:33.020
That was exhausting.

21:33.020 --> 21:36.470
Now I just want to take it 
easy for the rest of the day.

21:36.470 --> 21:37.500
What's this?

21:37.500 --> 21:40.480
Princess Mia, what happened to your hairpin?

21:40.480 --> 21:40.980
What?

21:41.440 --> 21:42.440
Oh...

21:42.720 --> 21:45.400
You're right. How strange.

21:51.150 --> 21:55.080
Of all things, I left a Lulus-made 
item in that forest?!

21:55.390 --> 21:56.630
Princess Mia?

21:56.630 --> 22:01.000
<i>There's no telling what might 
trigger the revolution!</i>

22:01.510 --> 22:04.300
I have to get it back!

23:35.010 --> 23:40.020
Illustration by: Yoko Fujioka
